#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186294151 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64b71f10-5b2b-5cae-a5dc-b9c160484d82" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Factored Polynomial Inequality"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "745f08d9-1eb8-52e3-94b1-fe8dac4c7444" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (0,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294153} {:answer/id #uuid "15335c6c-9de1-512f-8e37-6eea1794a3a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294154} {:answer/id #uuid "d33df2e9-e341-5866-82c4-64fea63b80a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-3,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294155} {:answer/id #uuid "ea9afecf-6a07-5501-bd32-35059b4a6903" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (0,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294156} {:answer/id #uuid "a3eda5c5-1086-500b-bb15-b55d2b8c5134" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-3,0)\\cup (2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294157}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "745f08d9-1eb8-52e3-94b1-fe8dac4c7444" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (0,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294153} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce80dd09-e6c0-5026-9933-9f24da3b1ce2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294152}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "91a16361-849f-5bee-aadf-8394f348cca6" :question/math-academy-id "q-116407" :question/problem "Given the polynomial $P(x)=x(x+3)(x-2),$ find the solution of $P(x)<0.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality $P(x)<0,$ we need to find the values of $x$ for which the curve $y=P(x)$ lies below the $x$-axis.\n\nThe roots of the polynomial $P(x)=x(x+3)(x-2)$ are $x=-3,x=0$ and $x=2,$ which are all simple roots.\n\nAlso, $P(x)$ is a cubic polynomial with a positive leading coefficient. So, we can graph the curve as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/assets/d87500612fc14636afa38bd01fdc1b90cf7eecd0bfbd546bff7b14d5a5b30fc8.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving $P(x)<0,$ we look for the part of the curve that is below the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x\\in (-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (0,2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186294158 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "48de9cc7-5f86-51e4-a827-796f77381af2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Polynomial Inequality Containing No Constant Term"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "399af956-c54f-5f1e-86b1-64b649a03fe7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-4)\\cup (2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294160} {:answer/id #uuid "c3b1efc4-4d5b-5699-bda0-1f4193c4524c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-4,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294161} {:answer/id #uuid "05747928-0930-55a5-a2af-3eca94075285" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-4,0)\\cup (0,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294162} {:answer/id #uuid "56ac85d6-fed4-5d1a-965f-542f9ecf6e1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294163} {:answer/id #uuid "7550b62e-23eb-5aa1-a7e0-55271b9683c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (0,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294164}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "399af956-c54f-5f1e-86b1-64b649a03fe7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-4)\\cup (2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294160} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9353a00-cc9b-570e-b83b-36de6f4e0e6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294159}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "88ba9665-3920-5271-b647-ee91ba660327" :question/math-academy-id "q-116439" :question/problem "Given $P(x)={x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2},$ solve $P(x)>0.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality $P(x)>0,$ we need to find the values of $x$ for which the curve $y=P(x)$ lies above the $x$-axis.\n\nFirst, we factor the polynomial $P(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x) & ={x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}({x}^{2}+2x-8) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}({x}^{2}-2x+4x-8) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(x(x-2)+4(x-2)) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(x+4)(x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe roots of the polynomial $P(x)={x}^{4}+3{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}$ are $x=-4,$ $x=0$ and $x=2,$  where\n\n- $x=0$ has multiplicity $2,$ and\n\n- $x=-4$ and $x=2$ are simple roots.\n\nSo, we can graph the curve as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/assets/a357caad0365f296f87367ee4ac1000f1ea772d0d27650c8340d475ca742828b.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving $P(x)>0,$ we look for the part of the curve that is above the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x\\in (-\\infty ,-4)\\cup (2,\\infty ).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186294165 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64b71f10-5b2b-5cae-a5dc-b9c160484d82" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Factored Polynomial Inequality"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec08760b-75b0-5905-8db2-722d7c9b31e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-2,-1]\\cup [0,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294167} {:answer/id #uuid "575cdb22-4e52-559c-8ca3-6b8610928980" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-2,-1]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294168} {:answer/id #uuid "1f02a4db-af53-5112-8cf9-64171dc99a23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-2]\\cup [-1,2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294169} {:answer/id #uuid "55d5cec3-6c39-58b0-a3f5-b3f3872eb40f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-2,-1]\\cup [2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294170} {:answer/id #uuid "5dedc4ab-ca7c-566e-b02e-0a596e0be473" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-2,-1]\\cup {0}\\cup [2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5dedc4ab-ca7c-566e-b02e-0a596e0be473" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-2,-1]\\cup {0}\\cup [2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294171} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1dcfc81-f413-5f1b-85f1-244fc0ae0c4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294166}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "339b5953-a820-57a6-b370-eaa9a986d779" :question/math-academy-id "q-40333" :question/problem "Given the polynomial $P(x)=-{x}^{2}(x+1)(x-2)(x+2),$ find the solution of $P(x)\\le 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality $P(x)\\le 0,$ we need to find the values of $x$ for which the curve $y=P(x)$ lies below the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nThe roots of the polynomial $P(x)=-{x}^{2}(x+1)(x-2)(x+2)$ are $x=\\pm 2,x=-1$ and $x=0,$ where\n\n- $x=\\pm 2$ and $x=-1$ are simple roots, and\n\n- $x=0$ has multiplicity $2.$\n\nAlso, $P(x)$ is a quintic polynomial with a negative leading coefficient. So, we can graph the curve as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/assets/1fb947e6360139669bae0821e0de8460da53ead628f589998fab1ce442646cdf.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving $P(x)\\le 0,$ we look for the part of the curve that is below the $x$-axis or touches this axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x\\in [-2,-1]\\cup {0}\\cup [2,\\infty ).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186294172 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "48de9cc7-5f86-51e4-a827-796f77381af2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Polynomial Inequality Containing No Constant Term"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c4073e8-f2fa-508a-9e58-9ac55da4fef3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294174} {:answer/id #uuid "c796b0ea-a4f0-55c1-b581-253020801a7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-1,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294175} {:answer/id #uuid "b723e3b0-c6c9-5e15-8974-6d270b7173d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294176} {:answer/id #uuid "eb2f7c96-343f-55b7-bf16-aebd7723db96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-1,0)\\cup (0,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294177} {:answer/id #uuid "e0ffb3bc-c9bb-5b86-9c1e-b56c06569d60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c4073e8-f2fa-508a-9e58-9ac55da4fef3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294174} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f189ece-3137-5595-951a-316be6645793" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294173}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8d4d2b0d-5f7d-59e7-b207-07fa5cc43dcd" :question/math-academy-id "q-40334" :question/problem "Given $P(x)={x}^{4}-{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2},$ solve $P(x)>0.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality $P(x)>0,$ we need to find the values of $x$ for which the curve $y=P(x)$ lies above the $x$-axis.\n\nFirst, we factorize the polynomial $P(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x) & ={x}^{4}-{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}({x}^{2}-x-2) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}({x}^{2}+x-2x-2) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(x(x+1)-2(x+1)) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(x+1)(x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe roots of the polynomial $P(x)={x}^{4}-{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}$ are $x=-1,$ $x=0$ and $x=2,$ where\n\n- $x=0$ has multiplicity $2,$ and\n\n- $x=-1$ and $x=2$ are simple roots.\n\nSo, we can graph the curve as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/assets/c0756761d00b0805683e447d8cee3b657bbbe004a0a47da428927585037b06c2.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving $P(x)>0,$ we look for the part of the curve that is above the $x$-axis.\n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x\\in (-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (2,\\infty ).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186294179 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64b71f10-5b2b-5cae-a5dc-b9c160484d82" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Factored Polynomial Inequality"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed1a1e36-e68a-5aff-b21d-3963066c9ec2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-2)\\cup (0,1)\\cup (2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294181} {:answer/id #uuid "dabba310-d4e4-5a16-bd43-a73d31cae5ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-2,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294182} {:answer/id #uuid "6b6e4308-cd2d-5294-890c-d1203cc620b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-2,0)\\cup (0,1)\\cup (1,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294183} {:answer/id #uuid "2d53e61a-6427-53e2-a9e6-b3337c00bd17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294184} {:answer/id #uuid "5ff58f0c-4a40-5382-857b-87ba433df160" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-2,0)\\cup (1,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294185}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ff58f0c-4a40-5382-857b-87ba433df160" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-2,0)\\cup (1,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294185} :answer-field/id #uuid "600f5eab-e116-59c9-b068-20d88170e956" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294180}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "616dc314-c0a2-534d-84d7-ac129ee2b412" :question/math-academy-id "q-40338" :question/problem "Given the polynomial $P(x)={x}^{3}(x-1)(x+2)(x-2),$ find the solution of $P(x)<0.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality $P(x)<0,$ we need to find the values of $x$ for which the curve $y=P(x)$ lies below the $x$-axis.\n\nThe roots of the polynomial $P(x)={x}^{3}(x-1)(x+2)(x-2)$ are $x=0,$ $x=1$ and $x=\\pm 2,$ where\n\n- $x=0$ has multiplicity $3,$ and\n\n- $x=1$ and $x=\\pm 2$ are simple roots.\n\nAlso, $P(x)$ is a polynomial of degree $6$ with a positive leading coefficient. So, we can graph the curve as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/assets/a37f1c62868581f74a60c073adabf59e2fc66cb17135ffa48df1c76eb22803c8.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving $P(x)<0,$ we look for the part of the curve that is below the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x\\in (-2,0)\\cup (1,2).$"}]}
